# Git Push + Deploy Workflow

- After implementing changes, prepare a git commit and push workflow by default.
- If repository/remote/deploy setup is missing, ask targeted questions to collect what is needed.
- Before any push/deploy step:
  - confirm tests or checks relevant to the change have run,
  - confirm no secrets are being committed,
  - summarize what will be pushed.
- If deployment command is known for this project, run it after a successful push.
- If deployment command is not known, ask for it once and store it in project docs.
